## Skin conditions: a modern-day problem that changes everyday life

Skin conditions are among the most common health complaints of our time. Psoriasis, atopic dermatitis, eczema or skin hypersensitivity can fundamentally affect daily life: from unpleasant physical symptoms such as itching, burning, pain or inflammation, to psychological impacts — stress, exhaustion or declining self-confidence.

Mariánské Lázně — now an officially recognised climatic spa — offers a comprehensive approach to treating dermatological problems that combines traditional balneology, modern medicine and the unique climatic conditions of the region.

## Why spa treatment helps with dermatological conditions

Spa treatment at Ensana Mariánské Lázně uses a combination of natural healing resources with a demonstrably beneficial effect on the skin.

### 1. Mineral baths

Mineral water with a high CO₂ content and other minerals helps to:

- reduce inflammatory processes in the skin,
- relieve itching and irritation,
- hydrate the skin and restore the skin barrier,
- improve elasticity and healing.

### 2. Carbonic baths and gas treatments

CO₂ penetrates the skin, dilates blood vessels and promotes:

- improved blood circulation,
- faster cell regeneration,
- softening and smoothing of scars,
- overall calming of skin symptoms.

Learn more about CO₂ therapy in Marienbad in the [guide to gas injections](/en/magazine/plynove-injekce-co2).

### 3. Peloid (mud) wraps

Peloids have an astringent effect, meaning they tighten the skin, and additionally offer:

- a bacteriostatic to bactericidal effect,
- the ability to suppress inflammation and promote healing,
- a positive impact on eczematous and psoriatic symptoms.

### 4. Climatotherapy in Marienbad

Since 2023, Mariánské Lázně has held the designation of a climatic spa — and for good reason. The local environment is characterised by:

- exceptionally clean air with low particulate matter,
- optimal humidity,
- low allergen concentration,
- stable temperatures without extreme fluctuations.

These factors help reduce inflammation, facilitate healing and support the natural regeneration of the skin. Time spent outdoors in fresh air also has a positive effect on mental well-being, which is crucial for chronic skin conditions.

## What the specialist says

MUDr. Lucie Jarešová, Vice-Chair of the Association of Outpatient Dermatovenereologists of the Czech Republic, on the effects of a stay at a climatic spa:

> "A stay at a climatic spa leads to improvement of skin symptoms thanks to the combination of healing treatments and clean air. The easing of itching leads to better sleep, which in turn has a positive effect on the psyche and on calming skin problems."

Her experience is confirmed by the practice of Ensana's medical teams: patients frequently report improvement not only in the physical condition of their skin but also in their overall well-being and a reduction in stress.

## Who can benefit from the treatment

The programmes are particularly suitable for patients with:

- **psoriasis**,
- **atopic dermatitis**,
- **eczema** of various origins,
- **hypersensitive or dry skin**,
- **chronic skin conditions** worsened by stress.

Each treatment plan is developed in collaboration with the medical team and tailored to the individual needs of the patient.

## Why choose Ensana in Marienbad

The combination of five key factors makes Marienbad one of the best places for treating dermatological conditions in Central Europe:

- unique [mineral springs](/en/mineral-springs),
- certified natural CO₂ sources,
- healing peloids,
- top-tier doctors and medical staff,
- exceptional climatic conditions.

Guests can also take advantage of modern wellness services, quality accommodation and a tranquil environment ideal for the regeneration of body and mind. An overview of [Ensana spa hotels](/en/accommodation) can be found on the accommodation page.
